                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "f48c11bf-7b87-465a-86b2-7aefb31a088f",
                        "entry_id": "e7faffcf-72cd-3b8d-b75e-5a048ffe2101",
                        "tags": [
                            "diminutive",
                            "neuter"
                        ],
                        "form": "sjappie"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "56d6679c-fbdd-3a0a-82e3-6c2cd75ae3e1",
                        "entry_id": "e7faffcf-72cd-3b8d-b75e-5a048ffe2101",
                        "glosses": [
                            "a nasty, anti-social (young) male, often considered uncivilized"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "derogatory",
                            "masculine",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cf01faad-9999-439d-a745-2c2ec7c995a1",
                                "sense_id": "56d6679c-fbdd-3a0a-82e3-6c2cd75ae3e1",
                                "text": "Natuurlijk is geld de oorzaak van alle moord en slechtheid, dat is bekend, maar waarom wordt de mindere man, ik bedoel de werkman, door alle sjappen als een soort dier aangezien?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "39d26573-42ae-4684-bcf9-5135d8e329a1",
                                "sense_id": "56d6679c-fbdd-3a0a-82e3-6c2cd75ae3e1",
                                "text": "1914, Israël Querido, \"Van Nes en Zeedijk\", in De Jordaan. Amsterdamsch epos, part 2, Scheltens & Giltay (10th ed. undated, first ed. 1914), 60.\nHet stonk er eeuwig en niks dan chappies zwabberden om je heen.",
                                "translation": "(please add an English translation of this quotation)",
                                "english": "(please add an English translation of this quotation)"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7d40efa9-33eb-3a6a-9735-c9fe61aef10d",
                        "entry_id": "e7faffcf-72cd-3b8d-b75e-5a048ffe2101",
                        "glosses": [
                            "a good egg, fine guy, trump"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated",
                            "masculine",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3a47e33f-b68b-43f4-9c0a-fb7ad6343975",
                                "sense_id": "7d40efa9-33eb-3a6a-9735-c9fe61aef10d",
                                "text": "Ach, het is eene kleine kunst, lijkt me, om tegenover elkaar te stellen de hyper-conservatieve edellieden uit een dorp - een graaf, een baron, een jonkheer, enkele freules - en een ‘rijken sjap’, zooals de parvenu zichzelven noemt.",
                                "translation": "Oh well, it must be an easy trick, methinks, to stir up the hyper-conservative nobles from a village - an earl, a baron, a squire, a couple of noblewomen - and a ‘rich trump’, as the upstart calls himself, against each other.",
                                "english": "Oh well, it must be an easy trick, methinks, to stir up the hyper-conservative nobles from a village - an earl, a baron, a squire, a couple of noblewomen - and a ‘rich trump’, as the upstart calls himself, against each other."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f7853da0-fe0f-470d-91cb-f3e8a8b340f8",
                                "sense_id": "7d40efa9-33eb-3a6a-9735-c9fe61aef10d",
                                "text": "‘Wat een goeie sjap was Theo toch; wat een beste goeie vent. (...)’",
                                "translation": "‘What a fine chap Theo was; what a great good egg. (...)’",
                                "english": "‘What a fine chap Theo was; what a great good egg. (...)’"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
